# Cargo build output for both workspaces.
target/

# rustfmt backups and merge-tool leftovers. Tree-wide: both workspaces are Rust.
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.orig

# Editor scratch.
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# Scratch from `make determinism` / `make gpu-smoke` (cleaned on success,
# left behind on failure so you can inspect the diverging runs).
.determinism-tmp/
.determinism-tmp.gpu.json
bench.json

.DS_Store

# Python bytecode from the Blender bridge (bridges/blender/**).
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Knowledge graphs are DERIVED artefacts, rebuildable via tools/graphify.sh.
# See memory/GRAPHIFY.md — the recipe is versioned, the 10 MB output is not.
graphify-out/

# Vendored third-party sources (third_party/) are deliberately NOT ignored:
# the LGPL obligation for planegcs is satisfied by shipping its sources.

samples/
instructions/
memory/

# Maintainer working notes. Ignored for TWO reasons, the second load-bearing:
#   1. consistency — `core-engine/notes_to_human.md` is already ignored, and the
#      root copy cross-references it, so committing one and not the other ships
#      a dead link;
#   2. it records live infrastructure access (a root SSH host, port and key
#      path for the GPU box). Publishing a `root@host:port` on a public repo
#      invites brute-force attempts even though the key itself is never in the
#      tree. If this file is ever un-ignored, REDACT §1.3 first.
notes_to_human.md
